2. MATHEMATICAL KINETICS & PHYSICS FORMULATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1 Solute Retention Fraction (f_s):
  f_s = exp(K1 * tau)
  Approximate: f_s = exp( -0.005013 * (CR_critical / CR_actual)^1.8 )

2.2 GP-I Zone Reversion Delay (t_reversion):
  t_reversion = 0.8 * (1.0 - exp(-t_NA / 18.0))  [hours]
  where t_NA is natural aging storage time in hours.

2.3 Effective Soak Time (t_soak_eff):
  t_soak_eff = max(0, t_furnace - t_ramp_lag - t_reversion)
  where t_ramp_lag = (thickness_mm * 1.5) / 60.0  [hours]

2.4 Shercliff-Ashby Hardness Evolution Model:
  HV(t) = HV_annealed + (HV_max - HV_annealed) * f_s * psi_NA * Fraction(t)
  Fraction(t) = (2 * (t / tau_peak)^0.5) / (1 + (t / tau_peak)^1.5)
  psi_NA = 1.0 - 0.05 * (1.0 - exp(-t_NA / 24.0))  [Natural aging penalty]

2.5 Thermal Stress / Shock Non-Distortion Limit:
  CR_max_safe = 120.0 / (1.0 + 0.05 * thickness_mm)  [°C/s]

